NAME
       arping - send ARP requests to a neighbour on the local network

SYNOPSIS
       arping [-c COUNT] [-I INTERFACE] ADDRESS

DESCRIPTION
       arping asks "who has ADDRESS?" with ARP (address resolution) packets on
       the local network and prints the hardware (MAC) address of whoever
       answers. Unlike ping it works below IP, so it gets an answer even when
       the other machine's firewall drops ICMP. Only machines on the same
       network segment can be reached.

       It is handy for checking that an address is really in use (or free)
       before you give it to a machine.

OPTIONS
       -c COUNT
              Stop after COUNT requests.

       -I INTERFACE
              Send the requests out of this interface, for example enp1s0.

EXAMPLES
       Check who answers for the gateway:

           arping -c 1 -I enp1s0 192.168.50.254

SEE ALSO
       ping(8), ip(8)
